+{
+  "file": "src/agents.ts",
+  "snippet": "  maxTurns: 5,",
+  "cause": "The triage agent, which handles every customer chat message, was defined without a session store, so Genkit rejects any request that resumes a chat by sessionId (only refundAgent had a store).",
+  "evidence": "Before the fix, triage.chat({ sessionId }).send('What is its status?') threw \"FAILED_PRECONDITION: Cannot use 'sessionId' with agent 'triage': this agent has no store configured\", and the check in node_modules/@genkit-ai/ai/lib/agent.js:329 confirms it. After adding store, a two-turn run on one session ('My order is A-1001.' then 'What is its status?') returned the A-1001 status, ETA and tracking code on the follow-up, and tsc --noEmit passes."
+}
